---
import Layout from '../layouts/main.astro';
import {products,productUrl,formatBytes} from '../lib/catalog';
const screens=products.flatMap(product=>product.screenshots.map(screen=>({product,screen})));
const total=screens.length;
const dimensioned=screens.filter(x=>x.screen.width&&x.screen.height).length;
const tagged=screens.filter(x=>x.screen.tags.length).length;
const documented=screens.filter(x=>x.screen.reviewStatus==='source-documented').length;
const review=screens.filter(x=>!x.screen.tags.length);
const formatted=(n:number)=>n.toLocaleString('en');
const pct=(a:number,b:number)=>b?Math.round(a/b*1000)/10:0;
const forms='https://github.com/mcmanussliam/screenshots-design-inspiration/issues/new/choose';
---
<Layout title="Dataset quality" description="Transparent information about screenshot coverage, provenance and curation priorities.">
 <section class="quality-hero">
  <p class="eyebrow">OPEN DATA GOVERNANCE</p>
  <h1>Dataset quality</h1>
  <p>Every original image is preserved at native resolution. We surface verified technical metadata, keep UI tags in separate facets, and label historical references whose sourcing still needs review.</p>
 </section>
 <section class="quality-metrics" aria-label="Current dataset statistics">
  <div><strong>{formatted(products.length)}</strong><span>Products</span></div>
  <div><strong>{formatted(total)}</strong><span>Original screens</span></div>
  <div><strong>{pct(dimensioned,total)}%</strong><span>With verified dimensions</span></div>
  <div><strong>{pct(tagged,total)}%</strong><span>With usable tags</span></div>
 </section>
 <section class="quality-section">
  <h2>What the metadata tells us</h2>
  <p><b>{formatted(documented)} screenshots</b> have individually documented capture sources and rights evidence. The remaining <b>{formatted(total-documented)}</b> historical images are retained as legacy references, not automatically presented as openly licensed. This is a provenance audit gap, not a claim that any specific screenshot infringes copyright.</p>
  <p>Technical metadata includes actual original pixel width and height, file format and stored byte size. The gallery uses consistent aspect-aware frames while preserving the originals.</p>
 </section>
 <section class="quality-section">
  <h2>Help improve the library</h2>
  <p>{review.length} screenshots are currently missing a usable screen or component tag. These are good candidates for a manual classification pass.</p>
  {review.length>0&&<div class="quality-review-list">{review.slice(0,24).map(({product,screen})=>
   <div class="quality-review-item"><a href={productUrl(product)}>{product.name}</a><span>{screen.name}</span><span>{screen.width&&screen.height?screen.width+' × '+screen.height+' px':''} {formatBytes(screen.sizeBytes)}</span></div>)}</div>}
  <p>The curation report in the repository also records cross-product duplicate images for human review. We deliberately do not guess which product owns identical imagery.</p>
  <a class="white-button" href={forms} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Suggest an entry or report a problem ↗</a>
 </section>
 <section class="quality-section">
  <h2>Tagging standards</h2>
  <p>Tags are separated into <b>screen types</b>, <b>UI elements</b>, <b>flows</b>, <b>UX patterns</b>, and <b>visual styles</b>. Synonyms are normalised and unknown legacy labels remain flagged for review. An automatically classified label is not considered human-verified without reviewing the underlying screenshot.</p>
  <p>Read <a href="https://github.com/mcmanussliam/screenshots-design-inspiration/blob/main/contributing.md" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">the contribution guide</a> for evidence, resolution, naming and image-rights requirements.</p>
 </section>
</Layout>
